{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7ac2c7ec9e5841f462fd548b2adbe08c1ec463d3900447ddd03e9345d1fe8c94","digest":{"component_or_area":"snapshot janitor / review-bot storage management","key_entities":["src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py:53","DEFAULT_FREE_WATERMARK_BYTES","src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py:303-345","_gc_pass","src/rebar/_config_sources.py","resolve_janitor_tunables","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","REBAR_GATE_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT","infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf:226","rebar-root-disk-pressure","src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:113","store_root","REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR","tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py"],"problem_keywords":["disk pressure","root filesystem","snapshot garbage collection","storage reclamation","review bot health","watermark threshold"],"propositions":["The snapshot janitor's reclaim trigger uses an absolute 2 GiB free-space floor that becomes unreachable on a 30 GiB root volume, only triggering at 93.3% used instead of before the 85% alarm threshold","Review-bot's ephemeral snapshot store materializes on the container writable layer because REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR is unset, and prune_docker_caches cannot reclaim running container layers","The janitor must engage at a volume-relative headroom percentage (default 0, set to 20 for review-bot) that scales with disk size and sits below the operator alarm floor","The reclaim mechanism requires hysteresis with a target margin above the trigger to avoid re-firing on every interval and must clamp the percentage knob to prevent pathological tuning"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":178736